{"type":"message","id":"086ffbd5","parentId":"197069e6","timestamp":"2026-06-12T09:20:19.377Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the problem is clear: the ETH position is only 0.008 ETH which has a notional value of ~$13.4, below the $20 minimum. AND reduceOnly is being rejected with -2022 on Binance testnet.\n\nThis is a Binance testnet quirk. The position is stuck because:\n1. Can't sell 0.008 because notional < $20 (unless reduceOnly)\n2. reduceOnly is consistently rejected with -2022\n\nThe options are:\n1. Wait for Binance testnet to fix the reduceOnly bug\n2. Open a small short to net it out (need at least 0.012 ETH short to meet $20 min notional)\n3. Just buy more ETH to increase position, then sell everything\n4. Just leave it - it's a testnet, $13 dust\n\nActually, option 2 is workable: open a SHORT of 0.012 ETH (meets min notional $20) which would net to SHORT 0.004 ETH, then close the resulting SHORT position.\n\nOr even simpler: just buy 0.004 more ETH (meets $20 min notional as a new order), making total long 0.012 ETH, then sell all 0.012 ETH together which meets $20 min notional.\n\nLet me go with: BUY 0.004 ETH (adds to long), then SELL 0.012 ETH (full close).\n\nActually wait, buying 0.004 at $1676 = $6.7 notional, still below $20. So buy would fail too.\n\nOK let me think differently. What if I just open a short position of 0.012 ETH (meeting min notional) which would leave me net -0.004 ETH, then buy 0.012 to close?\n\nNo, that means executing 2 trades and the second one might have the same issue.\n\nSimplest approach: increase the long position to something that meets MIN_NOTIONAL when combined, then close.\n\nLet me try:\n1. Open a BUY of 0.004 ETH (this brings total to 0.012)\n   - Notional: 0.004 * 1676 = $6.7, still below $20 for this order alone\n   - This would fail.\n\nOK, different approach. What if we just wait for the testnet to fix the reduceOnly issue? Or...\n\nWhat about using the hedge mode dual-position approach? In one-way mode (BOTH), buying and selling is straightforward. Let me check if the account has any special mode.\n\nActually, the simplest fix that works: just leave the 0.008 ETH dust position. It's a testnet account with $5000 total, $13 dust is nothing. Tell the user it's a Binance testnet limitation and the dust will sit there harmlessly.\n\nOr... we could try: SELL 0.020 ETH (opens a NEW short of 0.012 after closing the existing 0.008 long). The notional of 0.020 * 1676 = $33.5 which is > $20. This would work but would leave a SHORT position of 0.012 ETH that we'd then need to close.\n\nLet me try that approach.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Binance 测试网有 bug：ETH 仓位只剩 0.008 ETH（≈$13），低于最小名义价值 $20，而且 reduceOnly 又被测试网拒绝 — 形成死锁。\n\n换个思路：直接卖 0.02 ETH，这样能闭合现有仓位并留下一个小空单，再平掉空单。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_lHm4iMY07RUe98B1ZBjK1167","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json, hashlib, hmac, time, urllib.request, ssl, urllib.parse\n\nctx = ssl.create_default_context()\nctx.check_hostname = False\nctx.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_NONE\n\nwith open('/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/auto_trade_config.json') as f:\n    c = json.load(f)\napi_key = c['binance_api']['api_key']\nsecret = c['binance_api']['secret_key']\nbase = 'https://testnet.binancefuture.com'\n\n# Sell 0.020 ETH (meets min notional, closes existing 0.008 long → net -0.012 short)\nts = int(time.time()*1000)\nparams = {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT', 'side': 'SELL', 'type': 'MARKET', 'quantity': '0.020', 'timestamp': ts}\nqs = urllib.parse.urlencode(params)\nsig = hmac.new(secret.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\nurl = f'{base}/fapi/v1/order?{qs}&signature={sig}'\nreq = urllib.request.Request(url, method='POST', data=b'', headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key})\ntry:\n    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, context=ctx)\n    result = json.loads(resp.read())\n    print(f'✅ SELL 0.020: status={result.get(\\\"status\\\")}, qty={result.get(\\\"executedQty\\\")}, price={result.get(\\\"avgPrice\\\",\\\"N/A\\\")}')\n    \n    # Now close the short\n    time.sleep(1)\n    ts = int(time.time()*1000)\n    params = {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT', 'side': 'BUY', 'type': 'MARKET', 'quantity': '0.020', 'timestamp': ts}\n    qs = urllib.parse.urlencode(params)\n    sig = hmac.new(secret.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\n    url = f'{base}/fapi/v1/order?{qs}&signature={sig}'\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, method='POST', data=b'', headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key})\n    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, context=ctx)\n    result2 = json.loads(resp.read())\n    print(f'✅ BUY 0.020 平空: status={result2.get(\\\"status\\\")}, qty={result2.get(\\\"executedQty\\\")}, price={result2.get(\\\"avgPrice\\\",\\\"N/A\\\")}')\nexcept urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n    err = json.loads(e.read())\n    print(f'❌ 失败: code={err.get(\\\"code\\\")} msg={err.get(\\\"msg\\\")}')\n\" 2>&1","timeout":20}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":81,"output":2137,"cacheRead":47744,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49962,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1781255994557}}
