{"type":"message","id":"81dcd1a6","parentId":"88c087d0","timestamp":"2026-06-12T09:21:10.949Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see:\n\n1. SELL 0.020 - FILLED (this closed the 0.008 long and created a 0.012 short)\n2. BUY 0.020 - FILLED (this closed the 0.012 short and created a 0.008 long)\n\nBoth orders filled, but the net effect brought us back to 0.008 long because I bought back exactly what I sold. The sequence should have been:\n1. SELL 0.020 (close 0.008 long, create 0.012 short) \n2. BUY 0.012 (close 0.012 short, net 0)\n\nBut I did BUY 0.020 which recreated the 0.008 long.\n\nLet me also note the recent order history - there was a SELL 0.023 FILLED before. That seems like someone or some process already tried to close the position.\n\nOK let me try the correct sequence now:\n1. SELL 0.020 (closes 0.008 long, creates 0.012 short)\n2. BUY 0.012 (closes 0.012 short, net 0)\n\nWait, but BUY 0.012 * 1676 = ~$20.1 which is right at the edge of min notional. It might work. Let me try.\n\nActually, the recent orders show SELL 0.023 FILLED - that was from a different source. And SELL 0.020 FILLED + BUY 0.020 FILLED were my orders.\n\nThe current position is 0.008. My BUY 0.020 + earlier SELL 0.020 net to 0, but the position changed - entry went from 1684.68 to 1677.75. So my orders DID affect it. Let me calculate:\n- Start: 0.008 long at 1684.68\n- SELL 0.020: closes 0.008 long at ~1676, opens 0.012 short at ~1676\n- BUY 0.020: closes 0.012 short at ~1676, opens 0.008 long at ~1676\n- End: 0.008 long at 1677.75\n\nThe entry price changed from 1684.68 to 1677.75 (closer to current price), which makes sense - I sold at ~1676 and bought back at a similar price.\n\nOK so now I need to do: SELL 0.020 then BUY 0.012 to net zero.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"单子成交了但我买多了，回到了 0.008。正确做法是卖 0.020 再买 0.012 归零。"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_xRCIrn9jq94Z0QxvIcBV0971","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json, hashlib, hmac, time, urllib.request, ssl, urllib.parse\n\nctx = ssl.create_default_context()\nctx.check_hostname = False\nctx.verify_mode = ssl.CERT_NONE\n\nwith open('/root/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/auto_trade_config.json') as f:\n    c = json.load(f)\napi_key = c['binance_api']['api_key']\nsecret = c['binance_api']['secret_key']\nbase = 'https://testnet.binancefuture.com'\n\n# Step 1: SELL 0.020 → close 0.008 long, open 0.012 short\nts = int(time.time()*1000)\nparams = {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT', 'side': 'SELL', 'type': 'MARKET', 'quantity': '0.020', 'timestamp': ts}\nqs = urllib.parse.urlencode(params)\nsig = hmac.new(secret.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\nurl = f'{base}/fapi/v1/order?{qs}&signature={sig}'\nreq = urllib.request.Request(url, method='POST', data=b'', headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key})\nresp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, context=ctx)\nr1 = json.loads(resp.read())\nprint(f'S1 SELL 0.020: {r1.get(\\\"status\\\")} exec={r1.get(\\\"executedQty\\\")}')\n\ntime.sleep(2)\n\n# Step 2: BUY 0.012 → close 0.012 short, net 0\nts = int(time.time()*1000)\nparams = {'symbol': 'ETHUSDT', 'side': 'BUY', 'type': 'MARKET', 'quantity': '0.012', 'timestamp': ts}\nqs = urllib.parse.urlencode(params)\nsig = hmac.new(secret.encode(), qs.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\nurl = f'{base}/fapi/v1/order?{qs}&signature={sig}'\nreq = urllib.request.Request(url, method='POST', data=b'', headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key})\nresp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, context=ctx)\nr2 = json.loads(resp.read())\nprint(f'S2 BUY 0.012: {r2.get(\\\"status\\\")} exec={r2.get(\\\"executedQty\\\")}')\n\n# Verify\ntime.sleep(1)\nts = int(time.time()*1000)\nqs2 = f'timestamp={ts}'\nsig2 = hmac.new(secret.encode(), qs2.encode(), hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()\nurl2 = f'{base}/fapi/v2/positionRisk?{qs2}&signature={sig2}'\nreq2 = urllib.request.Request(url2, headers={'X-MBX-APIKEY': api_key})\nresp2 = urllib.request.urlopen(req2, context=ctx)\ndata =